+- **`trim` action**: Strips leading and trailing whitespace from the
+  concatenated value of `source_labels` and writes the result to
+  `target_label`. This is useful for cleaning up label values that pick up
+  stray whitespace (e.g. a trailing newline) from service discovery or from
+  concatenating several source labels together. Example: trim whitespace from
+  the `foo` label:
+
+  ```yaml {hl_lines=[1]}
+  - action: trim
+    source_labels: ["foo"]
+    target_label: "foo"
+  ```
+
